{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122669-dark-eras-useful-resources","id":1122669,"title":"Dark Eras: Useful Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T04:51:20-07:00","id":1122669,"title":"Dark Eras: Useful Resources","content":"This is a place to share resources that others might find useful to run a game in a certain Dark Era. This can be historical resources of any kind, or any other stuff that might be useful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Please try to avoid any kind of discussion to make this a clean list of recourses that is easy to use.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> Victorian Era (Gaslight) 1890, London <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> - Cthulhu by Gaslight (3rd Ed.)<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/100929/Cthulhu-by-Gaslight\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...hu-by-Gaslight</a><br /> <br /> - Cthulhu - Gaslicht (Extended, German version of the same book)<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/147007/CTHULHU-GASLICHT--Horror-in-den-1890ern\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...in-den-1890ern</a><br /> <br /> Both books give you a very good and solid historical background about everything that could be interesting for running a game at that time. The german version is a translated and largely extended version of the same book, offering additional historical information about certain topics that are not covered in the original.<br /> In addition to the historical background you get ideas for story hooks and some &quot;adventures&quot; for that era at the end of the book. Two in the english original and three in the german version. The english adventures were not translated, they are completely different.<br /> Even though these books were written with Call of Cthulhu in mind, they are a great recourse for everyone who what's to run a game in that era. In fact I doubt that I will need a second &quot;historical&quot; resource! So I highly recommend it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> Dark Eras 2<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> There is also a topic about recourses for the upcoming Dark Eras 2. Even though the initial idea for the topic is different, the resources might be interesting for storytellers as well:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112393-reference-and-research-for-dark-eras-2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...or-dark-eras-2</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ===============================<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> &quot;Dark Eras&quot; is meant as a general term here. The scope of the topic is not limited to the first Dark Eras book or it's companion. It's supposed to become a resource collection for every Dark Eras setting!<br /> Furthermore if it doesn't make much sense to split the resources for a certain setting into historical and modern resources, you don't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 07-30-2017, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T06:31:21-07:00","id":1122680,"title":"","content":"<b>Greco-Egyptian Naming Conventions: A Network Perspective</b> <br /> <i>Tags:</i> [Roman Egypt, Greek Culture, Ptolemaic Dynasty, Names]<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://grbs.library.duke.edu/public/journals/11/pageHeaderLogoImage_en_US.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293\" target=\"_blank\"> Graeco-Egyptian Naming Practices: A Network Perspective | Greek, Roman, and Byzantine Studies </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293\" target=\"_blank\"> http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is a neat little study on the origins of names in a series of second century manuscripts in Roman Egypt. In particular, it uses the connections between names names to reconstruct cultural patterns and compare/contrast between the Rural and Urban Societies. While it is CE, it is likely also a good source of inspirations for names during the Fall of Iserion Dark Era. <br /> <br /> ******<br /> <br /> One suggestion. It may be worthwhile to expand the scope of this topic to include both Dark Eras and Signature Settings. I know that I can provide some useful resources for the Dubai setting, for example, both historically and giving people a sense of what it's like to live in UAE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 07-30-2017, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T08:24:01-07:00","id":1122712,"title":"","content":"CNN 70s and 80s on Netflix are good cliff notes for the Bowery dogs and new wave requiem eras","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:30:46-07:00","id":1125329,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages (Celtic-Arthurian) Britain (Late 5th C)<br /> <br /> Keltia RPG, Age of Arthur, Mythic Britain (Runequest) - All three of these games are set in a realistic Celtic Britain with a wealth of background and information. All also take later aspects of the Arthurian legends that do not appear until the later Middle Ages but which we generally expect to be part of the story and effectively retrofit them into the realistic Celtic setting. The latter two games are available on drivethru. Keltia recently stopped being available there due to licensing changes but can still be found on amazon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:36:40-07:00","id":1125331,"title":"","content":"World Wars<br /> <br /> Weird Wars I and II - both great settings from Savage Worlds<br /> <br /> World War Cthulhu (Cubicle 7) and Achtung Cthulhu - Both games provide great background both for the historical aspects and supernatural ones of the time period. Achtung Cthulhu is a bit more on the pulpy side of things but still really useful. <br /> <br /> There is also a line from the same company that produced World War Cthulhu for the Cold War in the 1970's but I haven't checked it out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:47:50-07:00","id":1125334,"title":"","content":"Middle Ages<br /> <br /> Obviously the entire Old WoD Dark Ages line!<br /> <br /> Ars Magica - Great game now in its 5th Ed that has resources for petty much every area region of medieval Europe and near east. Especially useful for mage.<br /> <br /> Maelstrom - Originally produce in the 80's and recently revived this was a more gritty historical game set in 16th C England. Recently a spin off setting (Maelstrom: Domesday) was produced set in late 11th C England focusing on the city of York and surrounding area and focusing on supernatural threats to be faced by the heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","user":"scifirabbi","date":". 08-05-2017, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:54:20-07:00","id":1125338,"title":"","content":"Wild West<br /> <br /> Obviously Werewolf: Wild West for Old WoD. <br /> <br /> Deadlands Reloaded for Savage Worlds - lots of material for this dark supernatural world west alt history. It is an alt history and kind of pulpy but lots of great inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:47:24-07:00","id":1125397,"title":"","content":"17th and 18th C<br /> <br /> Both Solomon Kane rpg for savage worlds (based on the Robert E Howard classics) and Witch Hunter:The Invisible World rpg are world spanning setting in this period with heavy supernatural elements and focusing on fighting dark forces around the world. A Swedish game Lex Occultum has recently successfully funded a kisckstarter for an English translation of their game that will come out some time next year. The game is also a world spanning game of fighting against dark supernatural forces and is planning on having a campaign set in late 18th C Paris. <br /> <br /> Colonial Gothic RPG - los of info and background on fighting against dark supernatural forces in colonial and revolutionary America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:53:07-07:00","id":1125399,"title":"","content":"Golden Age Of Pirates<br /> <br /> Pirates of the Spanish Main for Savage worlds provides a lot of historical background and flavor with some minor supernatural elements. <br /> <br /> Buccaneer: Hell or High Water is another recently funded kisckstater also for Savage worlds that is set in a slightly alt history Caribbean in the golden age of piracy with some heavier supernatural elements. <br /> <br /> Also from TV the show Black Sails is basically a prequel to Treasur Island weaving a story of Long John Silver and Captain Flint into the stories of real pirates such as Blackbeard, Calico Jack Rackham, Anne Bonney etc. lots of action and political machinations that would make a great background for a vampire or mage game in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T01:44:15-07:00","id":1125516,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Use the edit function in the future instead of spamming posts. It's bad forum etiquette to make multiple posts one after the other when you can just edit your earlier post.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:45:48-07:00","id":1125595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122669-dark-eras-useful-resources?p=1125516#post1125516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Use the edit function in the future instead of spamming posts. It's bad forum etiquette to make multiple posts one after the other when you can just edit your earlier post.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry. Not a frequent poster so not aware of this etiquette. Other posters had posted about particular eras separately so seemed like the logical thing to do rather than one long post collecting lots of eras in a jumble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:34:02-08:00","id":1160340,"title":"","content":"Nerco to point out that Cocaine Cowboys, the ultimate documentary on the 80s miami drug trade, is now on Netflix as a resource for New Wave Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T13:18:10-08:00","id":1160950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122669-dark-eras-useful-resources#post1122669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-----------------------------------------------------------<br /> Victorian Era (Gaslight) 1890, London<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------</div> </div> </div> </div>(This is a little more broad than just 1890s London, covering from around the 1840s to the turn of the century, and looking at some corners of the British Empire as well as a few bits of America and France)<br /> <br /> Anne Perry's Thomas &amp; Charlotte Pitt novels, which start in 1881 with <i>Cater Street Hangman</i>, and her William Monk novels, which start in 1856 with <i>Face of a Stranger</i><br /> George MacDonald Fraiser's <i>Flashman</i> series<br /> Alan Moore &amp; Eddie Campbell's <i>From Hell</i><br /> Caleb Carr's <i>The Alienist</i><br /> James Clavel's <i>Tai Pai</i><br /> Michael Crichton's <i>The Great Train Robbery</i><br /> Eric Larson's <i>Devil in the White City</i><br /> Ruth Goodman's <i>How to be Victorian</i><br /> Chris Woodyard's <i>The Victorian Book of the Dead</i><br /> Tobias Churton's <i>Occult Paris: The Lost Magic of the Belle Epoque</i> <br /> Mary McAuliffe's <i>Dawn of the Belle Epoque</i><br /> <br /> <i>Zulu</i> (1964)<br /> <i>Khartoum</i> (1966)<br /> <i>The Four Feathers</i> (1977 or 2002)<br /> <i>The Limehouse Golem</i> (2016)<br /> <i>The Great Train Robbery</i> (1978)<br /> <i>The Ghost and The Darkness</i> (1996)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T11:30:07-07:00","id":1215562,"title":"","content":"Found today great site - Ancient.eu - that makes nicely readable in plain language articles on almost all historical topics. It's co-run with Oxford University. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.worldhistory.org/images/ahe-og-preview.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/\" target=\"_blank\"> World History Encyclopedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ancient.eu/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The free online history encyclopedia with fact-checked articles, images, videos, maps, timelines and more; operated as a non-profit organization. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:32:11-07:00","id":1221754,"title":"","content":"Found great page for marking of time relation to the world's geopolitical situation - <b><a href=\"https://www.timemaps.com/history/\" target=\"_blank\">Timemaps Archive</a></b>. Just point nearest date on the list and you can see how looked whole world in that time. Great visualization of context for historical games! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}